c(6, "§0.3; §3.3 N2; §8.1 #1, #3; §0.9 #1", "must-never-break", "The disclosure gap is externally corroborated: two say they were not told — 'L'app est bien mais il aurait pu prévenir que c'était payant' (1★); 'Kann sein das ich etwas falsch verstanden habe😭 aber man muss Geld ausgeben um die App zu benutzen, wenn nicht klärt mich bitte auf den die App wirkt perfekt' (2★ — a confused user asking a question who calls the app perfect: 'a rating lost to ambiguity, not to dissatisfaction'); checked against the listing — 'They are right': the description never states a habit-count limit ('Add, edit, and organize your habits in seconds'), names only subscriptions ('1 month and 1 year with 7 days of free trial'), and does not mention the $79.99 lifetime; 'the two things users complain about most — that there is a cap and that the cap is at N — appear nowhere in the material they read before installing'; MON_NO_DISCLOSURE 2 (4.88%, mean 1.50); §8.1 #1: state the limit in the description and first onboarding screen — 'Track up to 5 habits free, forever' — 'Zero engineering cost'; #3 reconcile the description with the SKU list", "listing silent on cap; lifetime unlisted", "1★-burst", "NO_DISCLOSURE 2 (4.88%) 1.50", "must-never-break", "limited evidence (corroborated externally)", "generalisable", ["12293956311","13606058398"])
